# 5 Sep 2026: no fixed diskcache release exists — the advisory's affected range
# ends at 5.6.3, which is the latest on PyPI, and it names no fix version.
# diskcache reaches the runtime set through dspy's cache (the LLM decoder made
# dspy core, ADR 0003). The vulnerability is unsafe pickle deserialization of
# cache entries, which requires an attacker to already have write access to the
# cache directory (`~/.dspy_cache`); in the shipped image that is the container's
# own filesystem, so it is not a remote-input path. Revisit when a release lands.
PYSEC-2026-2447       # diskcache         5.6.3   -> none released

